  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "dsh-emoji",
      "text": "[English](README.en.md) | 简体中文\n\n为 DeepSeek Harness 的回复加入可切换、自定义的行内表情和独立表情包。"
    },
    {
      "section": "效果预览",
      "text": "默认的大肥鱼表情：\n\n切换到贴吧表情包后，也能使用同一套语义协议展示贴吧表情：\n\n上传并切换到 B 站表情包后，也能保留熟悉的社区表达风格：\n\n同一套语义协议也可用于小红书、抖音、微博等自定义表情包。"
    },
    {
      "section": "安装",
      "text": "使用 DSH CLI 把插件加入 Web Profile，然后重启 Web Host：\n\n```sh\ndsh plugin --profile web add dsh-emoji\n```\n\n如需体验预发布版本，将安装命令中的包名替换为 `dsh-emoji@beta`。普通 `npm install dsh-emoji` 只会把包加入当前 Node.js 项目，不会启用 DSH 插件。"
    },
    {
      "section": "工作方式",
      "text": "- AI 想加入情绪或装饰性表情时，直接从 42 个允许的 Unicode 表情中选择，例如输出 `😊`；它们对应 40 个稳定语义，插件会在 Host 端将其转换为当前表情包的图片，无需额外模型调用。\n- 内置和用户上传的表情包共用 40 个稳定语义 key，可随时切换，并支持小、正常、偏大、大四档尺寸。\n- 转写只作用于 40 个规范 Unicode 表情、常见别名 `😄`／`🙂` 和本插件图片；其他 Unicode 表情、代码、链接、双冒号文本和普通 Markdown 图片保持原样。程序不会根据正文猜测情绪或自动补图。多张插件表情必须由有效正文分隔，相同表情可以在不同位置重复使用。"
    },
    {
      "section": "调整 AI 的表情频率",
      "text": "安装并重启 Web Host 后，打开侧栏「插件 → dsh-emoji」：\n\n- `关闭`：不使用表情。\n- `智能`：仅在表情确实有助于表达时自然使用，每回合最多 3 张，默认选项。\n- `高频`：在所有对话回复中加入一个合适的表情，并放在最能对应当前情绪的句子或短段落后；每回合最多 4 张。\n\n还可以选择表情包、调整显示尺寸，或填写“附加提示词”控制表情的选择、语气和使用场景。保存后从下一次回复生效，无需重启；所选频率策略仍依赖模型遵循提示词。"
    },
    {
      "section": "上传自己的表情包",
      "text": "在同一张设置卡片中点击“上传 ZIP”。上传成功后选择新表情包并保存，下一次模型调用立即使用，无需重启。自定义包复用内置的 40 个稳定语义 key；AI 仍使用同一组允许的 Unicode 表情，Host 只替换图片，不需要重新理解每套素材的含义。\n\nZIP 可以直接包含下列文件，也可以再包一层同名目录：\n\n```text\nmy-whale.zip\n├── pack.json\n└── images/\n    ├── happy.png\n\n表情包可通过 `displayMode` 声明展示方式：省略或 `inline` 使用行内表情；`block` 使用独立表情，AI 会被要求将表情单独成段，默认显示为 160px。设置页提供 120、160、200、240px 四档，独立于行内尺寸保存。\n\n`pack.json` 格式：\n\n```json\n{\n  \"schemaVersion\": 1,\n  \"keySet\": \"dsh-emoji-core@1\",\n  \"id\": \"my-whale\","
    },
    {
      "section": "上传自己的表情包",
      "text": "`schemaVersion` 表示 ZIP 技术格式，`keySet` 表示图片实现的语义集合。当前上传包必须声明 `dsh-emoji-core@1`；每个 key 的准确含义、相近语义边界和绘制建议见 [核心语义契约](EMOJI_KEYS.md)。\n\n40 个文件名 key 是：\n\n```text\nhappy, sad, confused, watching, angry, speechless, doge, overloaded,\nneutral, laughing, crying, sweating, thinking, okay, nodding, sleeping,\nhurt, peeking, approve, heart, shy, star-eyes, laugh-cry, touched,\nscared, facepalm, eye-roll, sigh, frustrated, playful, snickering,"
    },
    {
      "section": "上传自己的表情包",
      "text": "每个 key 必须且只能提供一个同名 `.png`。`id` 使用小写字母、数字和连字符，`version` 使用 SemVer；同一个 `id@version` 的内容不可覆盖，更新素材时必须提升版本。ZIP 上限 20 MiB，解压后上限 80 MiB，单文件上限 2 MiB，图片宽高均不得超过 512 像素；路径逃逸、额外文件、缺失 key、未知 `keySet`、伪造格式和同版本冲突都会被拒绝。\n\n用户包保存在 `$DSH_HOME/emoji-packs/`（默认 `~/.dsh/emoji-packs/`），Settings 只保存当前 `id@version`。从选择列表“移除”不会物理删除素材字节，因此历史消息里的版本化 URL 仍能回放；重新上传完全相同的 ZIP 可以恢复该版本。"
    },
    {
      "section": "兼容性",
      "text": "支持 DSH `0.1.7-rc.2` 与 `0.2.0-rc.2` 所属的 peer 范围（`^0.1.7-rc.2 || ^0.2.0-rc.2`），以及 Node.js `^22.19.0 || >=24`。本地开发固定 DSH `0.2.0-rc.2` 的精确类型链，部署时由 Web Profile 提供共享运行时；完整运行验收状态记录在 `package.json` 的 `dsh.compatibility.dshReleases` 中。设置保存到当前 Profile 的 `cordis.patch.yml`，表情素材保存在 DSH Home 中。"
    },
    {
      "section": "本地开发",
      "text": "需要 Node.js `^22.19.0 || >=24` 和 pnpm 11。\n\n```sh\ncorepack pnpm install\ncorepack pnpm typecheck\ncorepack pnpm test\ncorepack pnpm build"
    },
    {
      "section": "友情链接",
      "text": "已加入 [dshfind.com](https://dshfind.com) DSH 插件超市。"
    },
    {
      "section": "dsh-emoji",
      "text": "English | [简体中文](README.md)\n\nAdd switchable, customizable inline emoji and standalone stickers to DeepSeek Harness responses."
    },
    {
      "section": "Installation",
      "text": "Add the plugin to the Web Profile with the DSH CLI, then restart the Web Host:\n\n```sh\ndsh plugin --profile web add dsh-emoji\n```\n\nTo try a prerelease, replace the package name in the installation command with `dsh-emoji@beta`. A plain `npm install dsh-emoji` only adds the package to the current Node.js project; it does not enable the DSH plugin."
    },
    {
      "section": "How it works",
      "text": "- When the AI wants an emotional or decorative reaction, it chooses directly from 42 allowed Unicode emoji, such as `😊`. They resolve to 40 stable semantic keys, and the Host converts the chosen character into an image from the active emoji pack without another model call.\n- Built-in and uploaded packs share 40 stable semantic keys, can be switched at any time, and support four display sizes.\n- Rewriting applies only to the 40 canonical Unicode emoji, the common aliases `😄` and `🙂`, and this plugin's images. Other Unicode emoji, code, links, double-colon text, and ordinary Markdown images are left unchanged. The program never guesses the reply's emotion or inserts a fallback image. Reply text must separate multiple plugin emoji, while the same emoji may repeat later."
    },
    {
      "section": "Adjusting emoji frequency",
      "text": "After installation and a Web Host restart, open **Plugins → dsh-emoji** in the sidebar:\n\n- **Off**: do not use emoji.\n- **Smart**: use emoji only when it meaningfully helps express emotion, up to 3 per turn. This is the default.\n- **Frequent**: include one fitting custom emoji in every conversational reply and place it after the sentence or short paragraph whose emotion it best matches, up to 4 per turn."
    },
    {
      "section": "Adjusting emoji frequency",
      "text": "You can also choose an emoji pack, adjust its display size, or use **Additional prompt** to control emoji selection, tone, and usage. Changes apply to the next reply without a restart. The model is responsible for following the selected frequency policy."
    },
    {
      "section": "Uploading your own emoji pack",
      "text": "Click **Upload ZIP** in the same settings card. After upload, select the pack and save; the next model call uses it without a Host restart. A custom pack implements the same 40 stable semantic keys as the built-in pack. The AI keeps using the same allowed Unicode emoji while the Host changes only the image.\n\nThe ZIP may contain these files directly or inside one top-level directory:\n\n```text\nmy-whale.zip\n├── pack.json\n└── images/\n    ├── happy.png"
    },
    {
      "section": "Uploading your own emoji pack",
      "text": "The optional `displayMode` field controls presentation: omit it or use `\"inline\"` for inline emoji, or use `\"block\"` for standalone stickers. For block packs, the AI is instructed to place each emoji in its own paragraph with blank lines before and after it, and the Web client displays the sticker on a separate line. Standalone stickers default to 160px, with 120 / 160 / 200 / 240px options in settings. Inline and standalone sizes are saved separately. Switching packs does not change the presentation mode of historical replies."
    },
    {
      "section": "Uploading your own emoji pack",
      "text": "Example `pack.json` for a standalone sticker pack:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"schemaVersion\": 1,\n  \"keySet\": \"dsh-emoji-core@1\",\n  \"id\": \"my-whale\",\n\n`schemaVersion` identifies the technical ZIP format, while `keySet` identifies the semantic set implemented by the images. Uploaded packs must currently declare `dsh-emoji-core@1`. See the [core semantic contract](EMOJI_KEYS.md) for the normative meaning, visual guidance, and boundaries of every key.\n\nThe 40 filename keys are:"
    },
    {
      "section": "Uploading your own emoji pack",
      "text": "```text\nhappy, sad, confused, watching, angry, speechless, doge, overloaded,\nneutral, laughing, crying, sweating, thinking, okay, nodding, sleeping,\nhurt, peeking, approve, heart, shy, star-eyes, laugh-cry, touched,\nscared, facepalm, eye-roll, sigh, frustrated, playful, snickering,"
    },
    {
      "section": "Uploading your own emoji pack",
      "text": "Each key must have exactly one matching `.png`. IDs use lowercase letters, digits, and hyphens; versions use SemVer. Content at one `id@version` is immutable, so changes to assets or `displayMode` require a new version. Limits are 20 MiB per ZIP, 80 MiB expanded, 2 MiB per file, and 512 pixels per image dimension. Path traversal, extra files, missing keys, unknown `keySet` values, spoofed formats, and conflicting content are rejected."
    },
    {
      "section": "Uploading your own emoji pack",
      "text": "User packs live under `$DSH_HOME/emoji-packs/` (default `~/.dsh/emoji-packs/`), while Settings stores only the active `id@version`. **Remove** hides a pack from the selector but intentionally retains its immutable bytes for historical messages. Uploading the exact same ZIP restores that version."
    },
    {
      "section": "Compatibility",
      "text": "Supports DSH versions admitted by `^0.1.7-rc.2 || ^0.2.0-rc.2`, with Node.js `^22.19.0 || >=24`. Development pins the exact DSH `0.2.0-rc.2` type graph; the Web Profile supplies the shared runtime. Full runtime acceptance status is recorded in `package.json` under `dsh.compatibility.dshReleases`. Settings persist in the active Profile's `cordis.patch.yml`; image packs live in DSH Home."
    },
    {
      "section": "Local development",
      "text": "Requires Node.js `^22.19.0 || >=24` and pnpm 11.\n\n```sh\ncorepack pnpm install\ncorepack pnpm typecheck\ncorepack pnpm test\ncorepack pnpm build"
    },
    {
      "section": "Links",
      "text": "Available on the [dshfind.com](https://dshfind.com) DSH plugin marketplace."
    }
  ],
